# Copy to `.env` to override the defaults in compose.yaml.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Both values are read ONLY during first-time setup, i.e. while ./data holds no
# warpgate.yaml. Afterwards they live in that file and changing them here does
# nothing — edit data/warpgate.yaml, or delete ./data to start over.

# The address users will reach this gateway at, with no scheme and no port.
#
# LEAVING THIS UNSET IS THE SAFE CHOICE, and it is the default. Warpgate scopes
# the session cookie to external_host, so an external_host that does not match
# the address people actually type means the browser silently discards every
# session cookie: the sign-in page loads, accepts a password, and returns you
# to the sign-in page. Unset, cookies are scoped to whatever host the request
# arrived on, which is correct at localhost, at a hostname and at an IP.
#
# Set it when you serve HTTP targets, whose URLs are generated from it — and
# then make sure it is exactly the host in your users' address bar.
#WARPGATE_EXTERNAL_HOST=gateway.example.com

# Leave unset to have a random password generated and printed on first run,
# which is the safer default. Set it only if you need a known value.
#WARPGATE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
